# Source downloads: large, reproducible with scripts/fetch_*.py, never edited.
# Note the trailing /*: excluding "data/raw/" would exclude the directory
# itself, and git does not descend into an excluded directory, so none of the
# negations below could take effect. The workbooks already in the repo are
# there only because tracked files ignore .gitignore entirely.
data/raw/*
# ...except the Census of India C-16 workbooks. There is no API to fetch them
# from, so the build cannot re-derive mother tongue without them, and GODL-India
# permits redistribution with attribution. 12 MB buys a reproducible pipeline.
!data/raw/india/
!data/raw/india/c16/
!data/raw/india/c16/*.XLSX
!data/raw/srilanka/
!data/raw/srilanka/*.xlsx
!data/raw/singapore/
!data/raw/singapore/*.json
!data/raw/singapore/*.csv
!data/raw/switzerland/
!data/raw/switzerland/*.xlsx
# Kazakhstan's start-of-year ethnicity workbook: the Bureau's site is an
# application with no file link to fetch it from, and it is 380 KB.
!data/raw/kazakhstan/
!data/raw/kazakhstan/*.xlsx
# Korea's two registers, for a different reason: both hosts do have a file
# to fetch, and both answer a GitHub runner about one request in two (the
# rest end in a connect timeout), so a run that has once read them keeps
# what it read. A 75 KB zip and eighteen one-kilobyte CSVs, under the
# Korea Open Government License.
!data/raw/korea/
!data/raw/korea/*.zip
!data/raw/korea/*.csv
# Nepal's NPHC 2021 report, for the same reason: the census portal serves a
# certificate that is not valid for its own hostname, so there is no verified
# route to re-fetch it, and without the report the build cannot re-derive
# caste, mother tongue or religion for a single district.
!data/raw/nepal/
!data/raw/nepal/*.pdf
# Rosstat's Volume 5 tables, for Nepal's reason: its host serves a certificate
# signed by a state authority no ordinary trust store carries, so there is no
# verified route to the original and the files come from the Internet Archive
# instead. Keeping them makes the archive's availability irrelevant to a
# quarterly refresh, which is worth 2.6 MB on its own -- the earlier claim
# here, that the archive throttles, was a misreading of its playback wrapper.
!data/raw/russia/
!data/raw/russia/*.xlsx
# The 2020 U.S. Religion Census, for the same reason: there is no API, the
# US census is barred from asking the question, and without the workbook the
# build cannot re-derive religion for a single county.
!data/raw/us/
!data/raw/us/*.xlsx
# Afrobarometer R9. The published release is a 24 MB workbook of 400-odd
# columns; what is committed is the five-column extract the adapter reads,
# re-derivable with --extract. Without these two lines a clean checkout
# builds with no Afrobarometer at all and says nothing about it.
!data/raw/afrobarometer/
!data/raw/afrobarometer/*.csv.gz
!data/raw/afrobarometer/*.json
# Scotland's Census 2011 key statistics by council area, as published by
# National Records of Scotland. Three small CSVs; the 2022 equivalents are
# still behind a table builder, so these are what the map has.
!data/raw/scotland/
!data/raw/scotland/*.csv
# NISRA's Census 2021 MS-B tables for Northern Ireland, three of the ten the
# "Ethnicity, Identity, Language and Religion" release publishes: B01 ethnic
# group, B12 main language, B20 religion in intermediate detail. NISRA serves
# them as file downloads with no API behind them, and OGL v3.0 permits
# redistribution -- so without these lines a clean checkout has no Northern
# Ireland and no way to re-derive it.
!data/raw/northern_ireland/
!data/raw/northern_ireland/*.xlsx
# UN OCHA's Common Operational Dataset for Papua New Guinea: the 2011 census
# by province and district. Two CSVs, 11 KB, CC BY-IGO. They are the only
# count that can be placed on sixteen of the district shapes the map draws --
# the 2024 booklet is tabulated on a later district layout -- so without them
# a clean checkout has four provinces of empty districts and no way to
# re-derive them offline. See scripts/fetch_census/png.py --fetch.
!data/raw/png/
!data/raw/png/*.csv
# ...and the pages of Mongolia's 22 aimag census books that carry ethnic
# group and religion, laid out as text. The books themselves are 300 MB of
# scanned-quality PDF on the Internet Archive and the site that served them
# is gone; what is kept here is the few pages the adapter reads, so a build
# without network still runs. See scripts/fetch_census/mongolia.py --fetch.
!data/raw/mongolia/
!data/raw/mongolia/*.txt
data/processed/http_cache/

# Intermediate tiling artefacts
*.mbtiles
*.geojson.part
*.gpkg.part

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Node (only used to vendor the frontend libraries)
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Claude Code session state: agent worktrees and local settings, never project content.
.claude/
